---
import StaticPage from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../consts';
---

<StaticPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description={`How ${SITE_NAME} collects, uses, and protects visitor information.`}
  canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/"
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <p>
    This Privacy Policy describes how {SITE_NAME} ("we", "us") handles information
    when you visit this website. We are committed to minimizing data collection
    and being transparent about what we gather.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Log data:</strong> standard server logs (IP address, browser type, pages visited, timestamp).</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics:</strong> aggregate, privacy-respecting analytics to understand traffic patterns.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter (when active):</strong> your email address, if you choose to subscribe.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we use information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To operate, secure, and improve the website.</li>
    <li>To understand which stories readers find useful.</li>
    <li>To deliver newsletters you have explicitly requested.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies</h2>
  <p>
    We use a minimal set of cookies for essential functionality and aggregate
    analytics. We do not sell personal data to third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party content</h2>
  <p>
    Some pages may embed third-party content (such as share tools). Those providers
    may set their own cookies subject to their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal data we hold
    about you by contacting privacy@example.com.
  </p>

  <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
  <p>
    This site is not directed at children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect
    their personal information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected
    by the "Last updated" date above.
  </p>
</StaticPage>
